# Line-ending discipline for LFE adoption.
#
# Rationale: LFE upstream at your local LFE upstream checkout uses LF endings.
# Project-owned and extension files use the
# repo's autocrlf default. Locking LFE-SOURCE files to LF ensures future pulls
# of upstream LFE updates don't generate spurious whole-file diffs from CRLF/LF
# normalisation (the recurring landmine surfaced in VALIDATION_v2.md §5).
#
# Edit policy: this file is WI-pure project tooling. Update when LFE upstream
# adds new files in the LFE-SOURCE set.

# Default: auto-normalise text on commit; check out with platform-native endings.
*               text=auto

# LFE-SOURCE files must remain LF on disk (matches your local LFE upstream checkout).
.agents/permissions.json                                text eol=lf
.agents/adapters/system_prompt.txt                      text eol=lf
.agents/skills/**/*.md                                  text eol=lf
.docs/protocol/*.md                                     text eol=lf
.docs/protocol/personas/*.md                            text eol=lf

# Project-owned mirror of LFE skills for Claude Code dispatch.
# Byte-identical to .agents/skills/, kept in sync by scripts/sync-claude-skills.mjs.
# Drift is blocked at commit time by .githooks/pre-commit.
.claude/skills/**                                       text eol=lf

# Git hooks must be LF — shebangs break on Windows CRLF.
.githooks/*                                             text eol=lf

# Binary files — never normalise.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
